1	#!/usr/bin/env python3
     2	"""memory_index.py — build `project-memory/INDEX.md` from the entry files in `project-memory/entries/`.
     3	
     4	Run:  python3 tools/memory_index.py                  # write mode: rebuild the working tree's INDEX.md
     5	      python3 tools/memory_index.py --check          # check mode: rebuild from the staging area and compare
     6	      python3 tools/memory_index.py --check <rev>    # check mode: the same, from a commit
     7	
     8	One file per memory, one generated index over them. The index is never hand-edited: the same entries always give
     9	the same bytes (file names in code-point order, no date, no host, no locale), so "run the script and compare" is an
    10	exact check — the way Kubernetes and Cog keep generated files honest. Write mode reads the working tree; check mode
    11	reads git objects only and writes nothing, which is what makes the pre-commit hook safe to run on every commit.
    12	
    13	Do not edit `project-memory/INDEX.md` by hand — regenerate it here. When it conflicts in a merge, resolve the entry
    14	files, re-run this script and stage the result (G3.2). A test (tests/test_memory_index.py) runs `--check HEAD` on the
